        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-19T20:33:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "WDYT about adding the x and y offsets to InsertRecordingInfo?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 51,
        "startChar": 31,
        "endLine": 51,
        "endChar": 50
      },
      "revId": "7a016b0a05b5037a9ec8a1efdac68e022d387d92",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a0350d27_974d90ca",
        "filename": "include/gpu/graphite/Context.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 51,
      "author": {
        "id": 13824
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-24T15:13:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I didn\u0027t go this way here because I\u0027m wondering what would this look like if we eventually support arbitrary transforms? Would we have both a matrix and offset fields in InsertRecordingInfo, and if so would the offset fields take precedence?",
      "parentUuid": "530e8a55_4cb15aab",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 51,
        "startChar": 31,
        "endLine": 51,
        "endChar": 50
      },
      "revId": "7a016b0a05b5037a9ec8a1efdac68e022d387d92",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c2bfdf03_73fd209c",
        "filename": "include/gpu/graphite/Context.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 51,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-24T17:26:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we expanded to that, I think we could one of three things, depending on how much adoption we have and how hard it is to update clients:\n\n  - Define the precedence order so that both are defined, likely matrix and then a further posttransform integer offset. The matrix would default to identity so clients wouldn\u0027t need to be updated.\n  - Add a constructor for (int x, int y) that creates a Translate(x,y) matrix automatically; so clients likely wouldn\u0027t need to be modified unless they were assigning to the fields directly.\n  - Add a build flag that changes between the two definitions of InsertRecordingInfo and then migrate clients over. In all likelihood this would just be chromium.\n  \nI think there\u0027s a lot of ways to handle it down the road that aren\u0027t problematic, so I\u0027m inclined to keep the Context API itself smaller.",
      "parentUuid": "a0350d27_974d90ca",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 51,
        "startChar": 31,
        "endLine": 51,
        "endChar": 50
      },
      "revId": "7a016b0a05b5037a9ec8a1efdac68e022d387d92",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5f5e6197_2c6545d2",
        "filename": "include/gpu/graphite/Context.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 51,
      "author": {
        "id": 13824
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-24T21:59:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sounds good; put translation into InsertRecordingInfo.",
      "parentUuid": "c2bfdf03_73fd209c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 51,
        "startChar": 31,
        "endLine": 51,
        "endChar": 50
      },
      "revId": "7a016b0a05b5037a9ec8a1efdac68e022d387d92",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "80486f9a_3dace7c3",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/ContextUtils.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 334,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-19T20:33:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If/when we support arbitrary replay transforms, this would have to be `devPosition \u003d replayTransform * devPosition;`. Right now we pack the paint order Z in devPosition.z, which would lead to incorrect transforms, but .xy01 would overwrite any real Z and W values that came from an original matrix that had perspective.  We also would need to update the paint order Z to be multiplied by the final W after the replayTransform was applied. At the moment, no render step actually handles this correctly (perspective will actually lead to non-constant Z values for a draw and surprising results), so I think the contract for RenderStep\u0027s vertex shader would be to write a plain `float4 devPosition \u003d localToDevice * localCoord.xy01;`, then we apply `devPosition \u003d replayTransform * devPosition;` and finally apply `rtAdjust` and overwrite the .z coord with `paintDepth * devPosition.w`.\n\nThat said, since replayTransform doesn\u0027t have perspective and you\u0027re only modifying .xy of devPosition, you should get valid results. But thinking through what this might look like down the line, I realize having this extra replay transform makes analytic derivatives hard to adjust automatically. As long as replayTransform is a translation matrix, any derivative will remain valid on replay, but were we to add even rotation or scaling that would change. \n\nOne way to make that easier would be once RenderSteps use the standardized uniforms, we could always multiply replayTransform with the original localToDevice, so the RenderStep\u0027s VS code saw the final matrix magically. The only remaining issue there is dealing with bounding box estimates for clipping. After mapping to device space, it outsets by 1px to cover any outsetting that coverage AA might do and uses that to detect when things overlap. However, if we apply a scaling replayTransform, that 1px AA outset is going to change size relative to what we\u0027d been testing for when clipping.\n\nI don\u0027t want to give up on the dream of arbitrary replays, but between these new road bumps and the already known road bumps around dst readback, I wonder if we initially want to represent the replay transform more explicitly as just a translation?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 334,
        "startChar": 30,
        "endLine": 334,
        "endChar": 71
      },
      "revId": "7a016b0a05b5037a9ec8a1efdac68e022d387d92",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bbc557c1_a67423b4",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/ContextUtils.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 334,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-19T21:16:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I was talking with the AA outset challenge a little with Rob and we realized that scaling up decreases the device-space outset relative to the original bounds so that will never cause shapes to overlap. It\u0027s only downscaling that does so. If we have client\u0027s tell us their min and max scale factors for replaying we can conservatively still track draw bounding boxes.\n\nRob also agreed that we should probably keep the replay transform math/representation in the SkSL restricted to what we\u0027re supporting holistically. Having the ability to set a matrix on the command buffer but not having the rest of the system know how to handle an arbitrary matrix could lead to surprises. Additionally, if we limit ourselves to translations or scale+translations, the entire adjustment can be captured in the rtAdjust value I think. The scissor will still need to be updated dynamically since that operates separately from the viewport, IIRC.",
      "parentUuid": "80486f9a_3dace7c3",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 334,
        "startChar": 30,
        "endLine": 334,
        "endChar": 71
      },
      "revId": "7a016b0a05b5037a9ec8a1efdac68e022d387d92",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6edc05ac_b3528416",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/ContextUtils.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 334,
      "author": {
        "id": 13824
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-24T15:13:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Keeping this to translations for now makes sense. I hadn\u0027t been too worried about this part of the implementation, since I figured it was a work in progress anyways, but it definitely seems like a good idea to start with a minimal implementation that doesn\u0027t necessarily anticipate future functionality.\n\nIf we roll the translation into rtAdjust, as I understand that would just affect `rtAdjust.zw`? Looking at how rtAdjust is applied, do we have to worry about cases where `devPosition.w` !\u003d 1?",
      "parentUuid": "bbc557c1_a67423b4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 334,
        "startChar": 30,
        "endLine": 334,
        "endChar": 71
      },
      "revId": "7a016b0a05b5037a9ec8a1efdac68e022d387d92",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "368dfdaf_d43a2455",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/ContextUtils.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 334,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-24T17:26:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yep, it would just affect `rtAdjust.zw`, but I don\u0027t think we have to worry about `devPosition.w !\u003d 1`, since the way rtAdjust is appled ensures the position and dimensions of the viewport are effectively post homogeneous division.\n\nI think that means we could even just say that the replay translation is passed through as part of `setViewport(vx + tx, vy + ty, w, h)` but maybe it\u0027s easier to keep them separate until the command buffer is actually preparing the rtAdjust uniform values.",
      "parentUuid": "6edc05ac_b3528416",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 334,
        "startChar": 30,
        "endLine": 334,
        "endChar": 71
      },
      "revId": "7a016b0a05b5037a9ec8a1efdac68e022d387d92",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "372ec3e4_185cd9a9",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/ContextUtils.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 334,
      "author": {
        "id": 13824
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-24T21:59:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Well this brings up another idea -- if we apply the replay translation to the values passed in to e.g. MTLRenderCommandEncoder::setViewport, can we get away with not changing rtAdjust at all? Would this also work for scaling? Would you consider it better than using rtAdjust for translation and scaling?\n\nFrom what I understand, currently we always just set the viewport to (0, 0, target.width, target.height); at least I was operating under that assumption in this CL. Not sure if that\u0027s a safe assumption in the first place or if breaking that assumption will complicate things.",
      "parentUuid": "368dfdaf_d43a2455",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 334,
        "startChar": 30,
        "endLine": 334,
        "endChar": 71
      },
      "revId": "7a016b0a05b5037a9ec8a1efdac68e022d387d92",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "61c77cc3_63385a05",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/ContextUtils.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 334,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-07T15:40:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The viewport values that are passed to MTLRenderCommandEncoder::setViewpoert are the same that get passed down to the command buffer from DrawCommand::List/DrawPass. I do think for now we just always use (0,0,target.width,target.height) for the viewport at the DrawPass level but it could change in the future where we split content into multiple tiles that use grids of viewports so that encoders can run in parallel. On vulkan in particular, we can specify these bounds as limits on what needs to be loaded/stored to the target and I suspect that Metal does this automatically based on the GPU tiles that are touched.\n\nSkia likes to operate in the window/device coordinates and output pixels, but the GPU needs to consume normalized device coordinates from [-1, 1], which is where rtAdjust comes in. Assuming that\u0027s in-sync with the viewport then they effectively cancel each other out and Skia gets to keep thinking it\u0027s writing device pixels.\n\nIf we just translate the viewport but not rtAdjust, then I think it would be okay. Scaling should work out as well. There are two complications I can think of to look out for if you try it:\n- what happens to sk_FragCoord in the fragment shader. It likely responds to the viewport translation, but if a shader were to use it as the input to an inverse transform, we might get surprising results. Honestly, we probably need to handle that regardless of how the translation is specified, so maybe this is moot.\n- what happens when the new setViewport extends offscreen. I think then we\u0027d have to update rtAdjust accordingly.\n\nBut I think it\u0027s certainly doable and worth trying.",
      "parentUuid": "372ec3e4_185cd9a9",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 334,
        "startChar": 30,
        "endLine": 334,
        "endChar": 71
      },
      "revId": "7a016b0a05b5037a9ec8a1efdac68e022d387d92",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0a1fc2a6_158d71ea",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/ContextUtils.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 334,
      "author": {
        "id": 13824
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-07T20:50:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this is a pretty small (and possibly backend-specific) implementation detail, so I\u0027m not too worried about it (but let me know if you disagree). For now I changed the CL to apply the translation to the setViewport arguments.",
      "parentUuid": "61c77cc3_63385a05",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 334,
        "startChar": 30,
        "endLine": 334,
        "endChar": 71
      },
      "revId": "7a016b0a05b5037a9ec8a1efdac68e022d387d92",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4223cd29_055dc4fa",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/RenderPassTask.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 53,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-19T20:33:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Initially I thought we could skip tracking this and just always apply the replay transform, but then I fully understood your comment about saveLayers and that a given Recording could have render passes to a mix of surfaces, only some of which should be transformed.\n\nInstead of this, or passing the replay transform into addCommands, what if CommandBuffer (or something else) had a map from target to replay transform? This would let us naturally replay recordings even if they were always to the original surface. Any target not in the map would just see the identity transform.\n\nA possible variation on this would be addCommands() still taking the transform, but somehow the task graph can see what the target is, look up the right transform to pass in?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 53,
        "startChar": 9,
        "endLine": 53,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "7a016b0a05b5037a9ec8a1efdac68e022d387d92",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d031ab13_dbed43b5",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/RenderPassTask.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 53,
      "author": {
        "id": 13824
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-24T15:13:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is a map necessary? I think there will only be one target per render pass for which we\u0027d want to apply the replay transform. So maybe we could store that one target in the CommandBuffer, along with the transform, and only apply the transform to tasks with that target?",
      "parentUuid": "4223cd29_055dc4fa",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 53,
        "startChar": 9,
        "endLine": 53,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "7a016b0a05b5037a9ec8a1efdac68e022d387d92",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "42508a49_1d41545b",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/RenderPassTask.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 53,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-24T17:26:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That would end up looking like a loop over the tasks, and we\u0027d say if \"task is replay target\" pass in replay transform, otherwise pass in identity?\n\nI like that, although it would mean tasks need to expose a way of identifying their target. Once we have upload/copy tasks that need to respond to the replay transform as well, then we might have a better sense of how we could simplify (or not) this logic. Maybe it works out that the most straight forward approach is to always pass in the replay transform to `addCommands` and the tasks just know whether or not they should use it.\n\nOne thing that might make that last point simpler for tasks is if `addCommands` also took in the replay target, so a task could just compare then-and-there whether or not its dst or source proxy was equal to the replay target. I\u0027m okay postponing those decisions until later unless you\u0027re sold on one of these ideas and want to do it now.",
      "parentUuid": "d031ab13_dbed43b5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 53,
        "startChar": 9,
        "endLine": 53,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "7a016b0a05b5037a9ec8a1efdac68e022d387d92",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7fd6a654_8e19f640",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/RenderPassTask.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 53,
      "author": {
        "id": 13824
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-24T21:59:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Passing target and translation into `addCommands`.",
      "parentUuid": "42508a49_1d41545b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 53,
        "startChar": 9,
        "endLine": 53,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "7a016b0a05b5037a9ec8a1efdac68e022d387d92",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "98921e1d_19351d30",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/Task.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 31,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-19T20:33:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "wdyt about having addCommands() just take the replay transform, like it does in `TaskGraph::addCommands`? I think that gets the info in all the right places still but avoids the ordering requirement you mention in TaskGraph.cpp.\n\nedit* see more detailed brain storming in earlier comment.",
      "revId": "7a016b0a05b5037a9ec8a1efdac68e022d387d92",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fe387170_9cf08a86",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/Task.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 31,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-24T17:26:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Linking in one idea from 2nd round of comments, would be the `addCommands` functions take the replay transform and replay target as arguments. Or they take the actual InsertRecordingInfo? Or CommandBuffer lets you query the last set replay target and transform so tasks can query that if they are relevant.",
      "parentUuid": "98921e1d_19351d30",
      "revId": "7a016b0a05b5037a9ec8a1efdac68e022d387d92",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6e170bb8_bdce03aa",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/Task.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 31,
      "author": {
        "id": 13824
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-24T21:59:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I like the idea of consolidating the transform and target arguments, but using InsertRecordingInfo seems a little weird to me. Would it be worth defining a new type? This could introduce less noise into the `addCommands` signatures.",
      "parentUuid": "fe387170_9cf08a86",
      "revId": "7a016b0a05b5037a9ec8a1efdac68e022d387d92",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e814f2bd_41900793",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/Task.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 31,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-07T15:40:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, InsertRecordingInfo has too much other baggage on it. I think a new type makes sense. It could be an internal type or also defined in GraphiteTypes.h so that InsertRecordingInfo can refer to it.",
